===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|slang|intransitive}} To [[flirt]]; to talk or act [[amorous]]ly or [[intimate]]ly.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=Deontra Woods|title=Blood, Sweat and Tears|page=102|passage=I watched Brian as he drove off down the street. I turned and went back inside the studio and found Len at my desk. “I saw you and Brian '''cupcaking''' out there.”}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Michelle Robinson|title=Right Before My Eyes II|page=100|passage=But I figured Najah was '''cupcaking''' with Johan, Chelsea was eating something that didn't match while Greg rubbed her feet, and Kalena wasn't in a space to talk or listen.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2014|author=Zaneeya S.|title=Overcoming My Past|page=170|passage=She said, “You're always '''Cupcaking'''.” I replied, “I'm not cupcaking. I'm enjoying my conversation so hush.” David and I would stay on the phone all night and talk. It was normal for us.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|author=Mahalia Levey|title=Promiscuous Wolf|passage=“Luck is '''cupcaking''' on Myanna.”<br>His eyebrows shot up. “Cupcaking?”<br>“Old man.” She giggled. “Crushing. Your boy has a big time crush on Myanna.”}}
#* '''2018''', Carlos Bayne, ''Napkin Nights: The Crunk Chronicles''
#*: Let's review the tale of the tape: My best friend is being held hostage, I boosted his ride and mobile, then '''cupcaked''' with a heater-packing widow-maker.
# To mash a cupcake at; to cover with cupcake.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=T. David Lee|title=108th Street|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Eloquent Books|year=2008|pages=60, 169, and 199|isbn=978-1-934925-37-9|passage=After waving and smiling a quick farewell, I turned back on my way out of the lunchroom – and ran smack into Rusty Kuznevoy, flattening his chocolate cupcake against his chest.{{...}}Maybe he’d forgotten all about being '''cupcaked'''?{{...}}I recalled my vow of supremacy from last year, the one I’d made just before I '''cupcaked''' Rusty, and I reasoned that my science project could also bring me some redemption for the events of yesterday.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Rachel Hauck|title=A Royal Christmas Wedding|series=The Royal Wedding Series|publisher={{w|Zondervan}}|year=2016|pages=92–93|passage=So Colin crouched down, allowing her to smash a slightly used cupcake against his nose.{{...}}Avery took the aprons from him, carefully folding them so more crumbs wouldn’t fall to the already '''cupcaked''' snow.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Christina Hoag|title=Girl on the Brink|publisher=Fire and Ice|year=2016|page=11|isbn=978-1-68046-339-2|passage=She grabs another cupcake and quickly smushes it into the side of my face. I put down the camcorder and get her back. We’re now decorated in pink and white frosting. “I want a selfie of us,” she says. I pick up the camera and record us, '''cupcaked''' faces squeezed together, as we crack up.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Brian King|title=The Laughing Cure|publisher={{w|Skyhorse Publishing}}|year=2016|isbn=978-1-5107-0250-9|passage=Got any diabetes jokes you can share with readers? “I never got bullied the same as other kids—my house never got egged. It got '''cupcaked'''.” —Geoff Grant (Las Vegas, Nevada)}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Mandy M. Roth|authorlink=Mandy M. Roth|title=Act of Brotherhood|series=Paranormal Security®= and Intelligence® (Psi-Ops®) an Immortal Ops® World Novel|publisher=Raven Happy Hour|year=2018|isbn=9781947908048|passage=“{{...|nospace=1}}That was after I '''cupcaked''' him.” Dead silence greeted her. It ticked on for a few seconds as Nicolette yanked her cupcake-covered T-shirt off and tossed it onto her bathroom floor. “Are you there?” “Yes. I’m trying to figure out if I had a brain aneurysm or if I heard you right,” returned Clara. “Clara!” Nicolette squeaked. “I need your advice right now.” “On what part? The bringing-home-a-guy-to-have-sex-with or the Viking-cake bit?” “Not a Viking cake. A Viking ''covered'' in cake—erm, cupcake,” stressed Nicolette.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Alex Grecian|authorlink=Alex Grecian|title=The Saint of Wolves and Butchers|publisher=[[w:G. P. Putnam's Sons|G. P. Putnam’s Sons]]|year=2018|isbn=9780698407275|passage=“I '''cupcaked''' her.” “You did what?” “I '''cupcaked''' her. It was red velvet. I should’ve used a vanilla one, but I already picked a red velvet one.” “A cupcake.” “They had cupcakes for the birthday party. There was juice, too, but I didn’t have any. It had chunks.” “I don’t understand. What does that mean, you '''cupcaked''' her?” “You know, like I mashed a cupcake on her. In her face. Like at weddings and stuff.”}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Michael Casagrande|title=The story behind Alabama softball’s record 31-0 start|work=AL.com|url=https://www.al.com/alabama/2019/03/the-story-behind-alabama-softballs-record-31-0-start.html|date=21 March 2019|passage=The 28th straight win to open the season was greeted with cupcakes purchased by parents who made the spring break trip to Hawaii. “We '''cupcaked''' Murph’s face,” catcher Reagan Dykes said. “He didn’t seem too happy about that.” Confirmed. “I ran away from them too,” Murphy said. “I got one in the earhole. I smelled the frosting for like 12 hours.”}}
# To handle/succeed (easily).
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Mike Fish|title=College basketball — the power’s at…: UCLA rules, but ACC top conference|journal=The Kansas City Times|date=28 January 1981|page=D-3|pageurl=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/678114986/|passage=“Being an independent coach sure, I '''cupcaked''' my schedule,” said McGuire.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Jack Oakley|title=Modified battle is for 2nd|journal=The Register|volume=110|issue=221|date=19 July 1988|page=2B|pageurl=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/517784256/|passage=After John Garr popped out, Jeff Ward '''cupcaked''' a ball to short for a forceout and Black scored.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Kirk Bohls|title=A mere 56 years later, Aggies will take 2nd title|journal=Austin American-Statesman|date=15 April 1995|page=C1|pageurl=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/356879603/|passage=A&M also tackles Louisiana State and Tulsa and further '''cupcaked''' its campaign by arranging a game with Division I-AA Middle Tennessee State so it would have a sixth home game, moving Southwestern Louisiana back a year.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Keith Jarrett|title=Great record might not help Tigers|journal=Asheville Citizen-Times|volume=137|issue=346|date=12 December 2006|page=E4|pageurl=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/200541801/|passage=The Tigers have '''cupcaked''' their way to a 10-0 start against giant killers like Arkansas State, Monmouth and Charleston Southern.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Seth Stevenson|title=Who’d Pay £600M to Watch This?|journal=The Independent|issue=8,701|date=28 August 2014|page=38|pageurl=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/715266586/|passage=“I '''cupcaked''' the bitch!”}}
#* {{quote-web|en|title=Suns G Landry Shamet out through All-Star break with ankle injury|work=Arizona Sports|url=https://arizonasports.com/story/3025535/phoenix-suns-g-landry-shamet-out-through-all-star-break-with-ankle-injury/|date=14 February 2022|passage=“Competitively, I want to play yesterday. I know if I had to go out there and lace ’em up and everything was on the line, like, I’m doing it 100%. … Not that I’m '''cupcaking''' it or anything but you have to be a little smarter, take care of your body.”}}
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To cover or be abundant with cake-like decorations such as frills.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Lawrence J. Taylor|title=The Road to Mexico|location=Tucson, Ariz.|publisher=[[w:University of Arizona Press|The University of Arizona Press]]|year=1997|page=34|isbn=0-8165-1725-8|passage=Maeve joined them in happy admiration of the baby girl, who had just been christened with the name Genesis and was '''cupcaked''' for the occasion with endless bits of lace frill.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Joe Kilgore|title=A Farmhouse in the Rain|location=Winchester; Washington|publisher=Top Hat Books|year=2015|year_published=2016|passage=By nine o’clock that night the snow had begun to fall even harder. Brendon stood on the corner of 87{{sup|th}} Street and Stony Island Avenue beneath a green canvas awning now '''cupcaked''' with a layer of white.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Catherine Lowell|title=The Madwoman Upstairs|publisher=Touchstone|month=March|year=2016|page=271|isbn=978-1-5011-2421-1|passage=It was no longer light, but I still could make out the front yard, which was '''cupcaked''' in snow.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=David Poyer|authorlink=David Poyer|title=Onslaught: The War with China—The Opening Battle|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:St. Martin's Press|St. Martin’s Press]]|month=December|year=2016|page=18|isbn=978-1-4668-5983-8|passage=Ahead in the dim dawn rose the white '''cupcaked''' dome of the Capitol.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Stephanie Haney|title=The terrifying moment a bride nearly drowns as she gets stuck under her wedding dress after jumping into water before FIVE people come to her rescue|work={{w|MailOnline}}|url=https://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-4473822/Bride-nearly-drowns-gets-stuck-wedding-dress.html|date=4 May 2017|passage=It seemed like a beautiful moment as the billowy fabric '''cupcaked''' around her lower half.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To eat/feed cupcakes.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Fred Beck|title=Farmers Market Bulletin|journal=Los Angeles Times|volume=LXI|date=10 March 1942|page=2|pageurl=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/380721475/|passage=''So—we offered a cup cake a day for life to anybody who would find us a better word than the word “market.”''{{...}}She wrote to say that the Farmers Market defies description and asks why we don’t just keep on referring to it as the original Farmers Market and send the cup cakes to some home for under '''cup-caked''' children.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Kerrville Mountain Sun|volume=94|issue=48|location=Kerrville, Tex.|date=11 September 1975|page=six|pageurl=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/36362923/|passage=W[?] Ellis “'''cupcaked'''” her Decorative Stitchery group and [?] Barnett baked enough of her special bran muffins for all of the Meals on Wheels [?].}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Darry Madden|title=Opening her own business is icing on the cupcake|journal=The Boston Globe|volume=272|issue=88|date=26 September 2007|page=E4|pageurl=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/444292139/|passage=Ross, a pastry chef who recently moved from California, reels off half a dozen cupcake bakeries in the Santa Monica area she went to all the time, including one called “Le Cupcake” which opened last fall and prompted one food blogger to ask, “Are we '''cupcaked''' out? Is there room for yet another cupcake shop in Southern California?”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Coco Simon|title=Katie’s New Recipe|series=Cupcake Diaries|seriesvolume=13|publisher=Simon Spotlight|year=2013|page=42|isbn=978-1-4424-7168-9|passage=I love baking cupcakes, but I was starting to feel '''cupcaked'''-out.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Josh Lanyon|title=Bell, Book and Scandal: Bedknobs and Broomsticks|year=2021|isbn=9781945802973|passage=She slid a blue mini cupcake with green and teal sprinkles my way. “Try this Neptune’s Nibble.” I said regretfully, “I think I’m '''cupcaked''' out.”}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|informal}} To make cupcakes.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Gerald (Gunny) Gunthrup|title=The Gunny Sack|journal=The Oneonta Star|volume=LXIV|issue=657|location=Oneonta, N.Y.|date=23 December 1955|page=4|pageurl=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46365008/|passage=“I told ’em that you would bake us 30 cupcakes instead.” And so Mrs. Smith '''cupcaked''' the other night until 1 a.&nbsp;m.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Suzanne Thibeault|title=500 Things Project: Thinking about cupcakes and pickles|journal=TribLocal|date=25 August 2011|page=12|pageurl=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/232768207/|passage=And make cupcakes. I’ve '''cupcaked''' three times in the last few days.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Off Track Planet’s Brooklyn Travel Guide|publisher={{w|Running Press}}|year=2015|isbn=978-0-7624-5714-4|passage=While many a bakery '''cupcaked''' and failed, Robicelli’s continues to withstand the test of time.}}

